{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/833237-the-complications-of-a-high-cover","id":833237,"title":"The complications of a high Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T07:22:39-08:00","id":833237,"title":"The complications of a high Cover","content":"So, I'm about to play in my first game of Demon, and other than being INCREDIBLY excited, I've got a question: does having a higher Cover make it easier to risk Compromise? Does having a high Cover necessitate a more complicated life? I saw the book talking about how a low Cover Demon might have an apartment where there physically can't be one, whereas a high Cover Demon's apartment would be a regular thing. Stuff like that. But does having a high Cover mean you have a progressively more complicated &quot;life&quot;? Or can you be Cover 9-10 and be a homeless dude who doesn't have any friends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:17:58-08:00","id":833288,"title":"","content":"I think you have an excellent question, and I would like to answer it according to my reading of cover which may or may not be correct XD<br /> <br /> At first, to my understanding you couldn't be a homeless dude with no friends and have a cover 9-10. I think that guy you mentioned would be a cover rating of 4 because cover means how smooth can you pass by as a human to agents of the Machine.<br /> But when you come to think of it, how often does anyone look twice to a homeless guy in the streets? I'd say he is like the perfect spy, in the sense that he can observe people on the street being close to invisible. HOWEVER, the moment the homeless guy enter any place he becomes pretty much the CENTER of attention: people have prejudice and are expecting him to rob the place or something like that. But since there is no such thing as conditional cover, I would rule it would stay on the 4 rating. <br /> <br /> But this again, is not necessarily bad, for it would minimize a lot compromise rolls due to acting out of character. No one knows him, so how could anyone say if he is acting as expected or not? <br /> On the other hand, his cover would erode quickly when coming for compromise rolls due to powers and demonic forms. Also he is more prone to fail on spoofing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now on the other hand high covers, they can be very different but they all come with social costs. <br /> Like high cover means you have a very detailed and public (to an extent) life. meaning: For me a 10 cover would be The guy who is divorced but now remarried and having 2 children and a dog. He goes out every friday for a happy hour, he is the manager in a bank and has several clients on first name basis, and might play golf on sundays with his brother-in-law.<br /> He is pretty much inivisble in all situations.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that he would often have to do compromise rolls due to acting out of character: there are several expectations on how he should act. On the other hand he has a beautiful dice pool for spoofing AND using demonic forms and powers. He can use those power quite often without risking much. <br /> <br /> But you could also have a very high cover like: Daisy Ridley<br /> Until last year no one really knew you and then: BAN! Star WARS!<br /> You may not have a lot of friends or people in your life but you are in the eye of millions of people (perhaps billions?). I know nothing from her personal life, not even how old she is, but if she does anything remotely strange she would go right away for the magazines and that is the trade of in that case. <br /> <br /> So anyway, these are my two cents ^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T09:27:38-08:00","id":833339,"title":"","content":"High Cover rating pretty much have to come from somewhere. A Demon's original starts at 7 - to get any higher, you need to Pact in pieces from other people, and those pieces are nearly always social (in some manner). Patch-Jobs are the above, but <i>even more</i>. A Soul Pact can net you a really high Cover, but you are assuming all the original's social links and obligations. Angel Jacking is variable, but you still have to abide by the original's behavioral specifications.<br /> <br /> <i>Less</i> social constraints can be had through identifiers, as opposed to relationships, such as the example of a drug habit, or noticeable behavior. Remember though: the entire point of Cover is acting as a convincing alibi stating &quot;yes, I exist and am a perfectly normal human. Here are my references.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:02:23-08:00","id":833361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/833237-the-complications-of-a-high-cover?p=833339#post833339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Cover rating pretty much have to come from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> They often <i>do</i>, because demons run into the same paranoid traps as changelings do when it comes to balancing supernatural power and mortal connections, but it's entirely possible for a demon to build their way to Cover 10 without making a single pact. Being subtle takes longer but pays in a life that doesn't cost you chunks of Willpower and worry over the security of a filing cabinet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:44:00-08:00","id":833417,"title":"","content":"Living your cover is a good option, one that many Demons do use in the long term.<br /> <br /> Also, not all Cover obligations are created equal. If a Demons, say, buy <i>all</i> of the friendships a person had as, say a kindergartner, that probably adds up to one, <i>maybe</i> two cover XP, if the Storyteller is feeling generous for the &quot;Buy in bulk&quot; aspect, but now that Demon has a wide range of people who remember them &quot;as a child&quot; in case anyone tries to degrade their cover through research(also useful for trying to create the Established condition for a cover), and their obligations to these people consist of running into them, once in a lifetime, at grocery store and saying &quot;Hey, I remember you from Trent Children's Academy! How have you been?&quot;<br /> <br /> Same thing for college boyfriend/girlfriend/roommates, former employers, etc. etc. There are plenty of opportunity to fill in gaps in your Cover that don't force you spend your excessive time and energy maintaining relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:59:36-08:00","id":833542,"title":"","content":"My romance with demon was short, but the way i envisioned high cover working was that you give a lot of signals that give your cover credit. Imagine that if a GM is passively Processing a lot of info about your charakter, there is a lot of stuff in it that make idea of &quot;its a demon&quot; improbable and looking luk\u0119 statistical error. And because GM is Processing a lot of random shit, by spoon feeding it data like this you use its methodology against it. So a high cover homeless dude should be one that is visibly homeless, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:39:19-08:00","id":833709,"title":"","content":"I will throw a question at the board related to this.<br /> <br /> I am planning to run a game set during the crusades. One of my players is playing a demon whose cover is a spy for the Hebrew community in Jerusalem. He basically spies on people for a powerful Rabbi. <br /> <br /> I liked the concept a lot because it fit the themes, however it sort of weird to handle because his cover to the God Machine is &quot;Oh look at me, I am just a Jew spying on French Crusaders&quot;. <br /> <br /> Should covers like this take any special considerations? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:41:53-08:00","id":833711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/833237-the-complications-of-a-high-cover?p=833709#post833709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will throw a question at the board related to this.<br /> <br /> I am planning to run a game set during the crusades. One of my players is playing a demon whose cover is a spy for the Hebrew community in Jerusalem. He basically spies on people for a powerful Rabbi.<br /> <br /> I liked the concept a lot because it fit the themes, however it sort of weird to handle because his cover to the God Machine is &quot;Oh look at me, I am just a Jew spying on French Crusaders&quot;.<br /> <br /> Should covers like this take any special considerations?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Alternate Identity seems readily suitable for a spy Cover and has effects that bear consideration in any game where the threat of Cover degradation from investigation is a significant aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T07:58:50-08:00","id":833835,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras Berlin deals with the complications of having a Cover that works as a spy. Check out the draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}